write('docs/PR-AUTOTRACK-RETIREMENT.md','''# Automatic PR indexing is retired

TraceDecay no longer discovers every open pull request, fetches its head into a
synthetic ref, or creates and reconciles a linked checkout in the background.
There is no replacement poller, implicit all-PR queue, or automatic cleanup sweep.

## Inspect a requested branch

Use `tracedecay branch add <branch> --path <project>` to request an exact local
branch head. This retains the existing branch lifecycle lease, scheduler
admission, source provenance, and typed warming/unavailable results. Normal
GitHub review and CI evidence, PR context, linked worktrees, and Work-managed
execution remain supported. This retirement does not grant access to a fork or
fetch arbitrary remote code on an agent's behalf.

`branch autotrack` is no longer a CLI command. The configuration registry no
longer advertises or accepts `sync.auto_track_pr_branches.v1` or
`sync.auto_track_pr_poll_secs.v1`. The dashboard has no automatic-PR toggle,
poll interval, or managed-PR summary. Retired project PATCH fields are rejected,
not ignored. Incompatible persisted configuration follows the existing typed
reset/refusal policy; there is no silent reinterpretation or new migration.

## Existing artifacts are preserved

Retiring the product is not permission to delete an existing checkout. Neither
startup nor a setting change removes old `pr-worktrees`, synthetic refs, branch
records, or shared project/session data. The old `pr-autotrack.json` writer is
gone. No compatibility runtime reads that file to resume automatic indexing.

Doctor reads an existing inventory only to report its exact recorded branch,
source branch, worktree, tracking ref, and head. It explicitly distinguishes a
record from a current ownership proof. An unreadable or invalid inventory is
reported and preserved; a directory with a similar name is not discovered or
claimed by a prefix sweep.

Cleanup requires operator review and the existing daemon-owned branch
lifecycle. Keep the recorded inventory until the corresponding routes and
artifacts have been reconciled. Verify the repository, current HEAD and refs,
worktree cleanliness, and active leases before any retirement. Preserve dirty,
foreign, or currently leased artifacts. Do not force-remove a checkout or
recursively delete a project store merely because its name contains a PR
number. Doctor's inventory is not an automatic reclamation command and does
not claim that an artifact is safe to remove.
''')
print('authored retirement complete')

